                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_03\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix adds a default value to BddRunContext.runningBatchKey\n(\"Optional.of(\"batch-1\")\"), with the comment \"must be initialized for\njbehave-junit-runner\", because the field could previously be read\n(via getRunningBatchKey()/getRunningBatch()) before any batch was\nactually started, causing an exception (reported as NPE) when\njbehave-junit-runner builds the JUnit execution tree ahead of the\nreal story execution.\n\nThe `runningBatchKey` field itself was declared uninitialized all the\nway back in candidate_01 (the initial creation of BddRunContext), but\nit was harmless at that point: the only consumer, getRunningBatch(),\nwas called from step implementations that only ever execute during an\nactual, already-running batch.\n\ncandidate_03 is the commit that changes this. It refactors\nBddRunContext to expose a new getRunningBatchKey() method and, more\nimportantly, modifies VariablesFactory so that createVariables() now\nunconditionally calls bddRunContext.getRunningBatchKey() to merge in\nbatch-scoped variables:\n\n    globalScoped.putAll(batchVariables.getOrDefault(bddRunContext.getRunningBatchKey(), Map.of()));\n\nBefore this commit, VariablesFactory had no dependency at all on\nIBddRunContext (its constructor only took an IPropertyParser). After\nthis commit, every call to createVariables() requires a running batch\nto already be set, throwing IllegalStateException/NPE otherwise. Since\njbehave-junit-runner builds its JUnit execution tree (which triggers\nvariable/step resolution) before any batch is started via\nputRunningBatch(), this is exactly the failure path described in the\nfix commit message. This new, unconditional dependency introduced in\ncandidate_03 is what actually turned the previously-harmless\nuninitialized field into a real bug, and it is fixed by initializing\nthe field with a safe default in the fix commit.\n\nNone of the later candidates (04, 05) touch this call path or the\nfield's initialization \u2014 they only refactor batch storage classes\naround it \u2014 so candidate_03 is the first commit that introduced the\nproblematic code exercised by the fix.\n"
                }
              }
            ]
          },
